# Frontend Rules

## Existing Frontend

- The current frontend is a usable baseline.
- Preserve the existing layout.
- Preserve the existing navigation.
- Preserve the existing theme.
- Preserve existing working components.
- Do not redesign a page when the task only requires API integration.
- Do not replace a working component without a documented reason.
- Reuse existing components before creating new components.

## API Integration

- Follow `docs/03_API_CONTRACT.yaml`.
- Do not silently rename backend response fields.
- Use the existing API client if one already exists.
- Otherwise create one shared API client.
- Do not call the backend directly from many unrelated components.
- Do not hard-code the backend URL inside components.
- Store environment-specific URLs in environment configuration.
- Attach JWT using the shared authentication mechanism.
- Handle `401 Unauthorized` consistently.
- Handle `403 Forbidden` consistently.

## Data States

Every data-driven page must support applicable states:

- Loading.
- Empty.
- Validation error.
- API error.
- Retry.
- Disabled while submitting.
- Success feedback.

Do not display stale mock data after an API request fails.

## Mock Data

- Keep mock services replaceable.
- Remove mock data only after the real API flow works.
- Do not silently mix mock and real data.
- The task file must state whether mock or real API is being used.
- Mock DTOs must match the real OpenAPI contract.

## TypeScript

- Create TypeScript DTOs that match OpenAPI.
- Do not use `any` for stable API contracts.
- Keep enum values identical to backend values.
- Do not duplicate the same DTO across many components.
- Parse date-time values explicitly when needed.
- Do not assume nullable fields are always present.

## Forms

- Validate required fields.
- Show field-level validation where appropriate.
- Prevent duplicate submissions.
- Disable submit while processing.
- Preserve user input when a recoverable request fails.

## Security and Privacy

- Do not log access tokens.
- Do not log sensitive chat content.
- Do not persist sensitive content in localStorage unless explicitly required.
- Hidden buttons are not authorization.
- Backend authorization remains mandatory.
- Do not expose admin actions to normal users through route mistakes.

## Scope

- Modify only pages, services and types required by the current task.
- Do not perform broad frontend refactoring during a small integration task.
- Do not replace the existing design system without approval.
- Run type-check.
- Run production build.
- Report the exact command and actual result.